  <static seed="219" source="Contrib/DMOI/2-Sequences/2_6-Chapter_Summary/2_6_3.pg">
    <statement><p>Consider the sequence given by <m>a_n = 3\cdot 5^{n-1}\text{.}</m></p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p>Find the first 4 terms of the sequence.</p>
<p><m>a_1 =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, <m>a_2 =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, <m>a_3 =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0003"/>, <m>a_4 =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0004"/> ,...</p>
<p>What sort of sequence is this?</p>
<p><ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0005"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>arithmetic</p>
</li><li>
<p>geometric</p>
</li><li>
<p>neither</p>
</li></ul></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Find the <em>sum</em> of the first 21 terms. That is, compute <m>\sum_{k=1}^{21}a_k\text{.}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>15</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>75</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>375</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{geometric}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{3\cdot 5^{21}-3}{4}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>3, 15, 75, 375, \ldots</m> The sequence is geometric.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\frac{3\cdot5^{21}-3}{4}={3.57628\times 10^{14}}\text{.}</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</solution>
